NAME
====

**augite-repo** - generate a static site for a Git repository

SYNOPSIS
========

**augite repo** [**-o** _dir_ | **--output** _dir_]
                [**-g** _dir_ | **--grammars** _dir_]
                [**-c** _dir_ | **--cache** _dir_]
                [**-p** _number_ | **--per-page** _number_]
                [**-u** _url_ | **--base-url** _url_]
                [**--parent** _path_] _repo-dir_

DESCRIPTION
===========

**augite repo** generates a site for the Git repository at _repo-dir_.
The site includes a paginated commit log, commit diffs, the files at HEAD,
branches, tags and Atom feeds. Repository metadata can be set with
`augite-setup(1)`.

The output directory is created if necessary and defaults to the current
directory. Log pages, file pages, references, feeds, the stylesheet and
JavaScript are updated on each run. Pages for files no longer in the tree
and log pages beyond the last page are removed.

Commit pages are written only when they do not already exist. To regenerate
all commit pages after an upgrade, remove the output directory's `commit/`
subdirectory and run the command again.

OPTIONS
=======

- **-o**, **--output** _dir_:
  Writes the site to _dir_ instead of the current directory.

- **-g**, **--grammars** _dir_:
  Uses TextMate grammars in _dir_ to highlight file pages. Without this
  option, file pages are plain text. To add a language, copy its
  ``.tmLanguage.json`` file into the directory.

- **-c**, **--cache** _dir_:
  Keeps highlighted files in _dir_ between runs to avoid highlighting them
  again. The directory is created if necessary. Changes to the grammars
  invalidate cached highlighting. Unused cache files are removed after a run.

- **-p**, **--per-page** _number_:
  Sets the number of commits per log page. The default is 50. The number
  must be a positive integer.

- **-u**, **--base-url** _url_:
  Sets the site's base URL, used to make links in the Atom feeds absolute.
  For example, ``https://code.example.org/engine/``. Without this option,
  feed links are relative. This is separate from the clone URL set by
  `augite-setup(1)`.

- **--parent** _path_:
  Links each page to the list of repositories at _path_, such as one written
  by `augite-index(1)`. A relative _path_ is relative to the site's root, so
  ``..`` is the directory above it. An absolute path or a URL is used as is.
  The link appears above the header and on the logo. Without this option,
  pages do not link outside the site.

- **-h**, **--help**:
  Prints a usage summary and exits.

FILES
=====

Paths below are relative to the output directory.

- `./index.html`, `./log.html`, `./log/<number>.html`:
  The commit log. The first page is written to both ``index.html`` and
  ``log.html``; subsequent pages are written under `log/`.

- `./commit/<hash>.html`:
  Individual commit pages.

- `./files.html`, `./file/`:
  The file listing and individual file pages.

- `./refs.html`:
  Branches and tags.

- `./atom.xml`, `./tags.xml`:
  Atom feeds for the latest 100 commits and for tags.

- `./style.css`, `./augite.js`:
  The stylesheet and JavaScript used by the site.

- `./logo.png`, `./favicon.png`:
  Images linked by the pages. Augite does not create these files; supply
  them separately.

EXAMPLES
========

Generate a site with syntax highlighting and a persistent highlighting cache:

````
$ augite repo -o public/engine -g grammars -c cache/engine \
    -u https://code.example.org/engine/ --parent .. \
    /var/git/engine.git
````

To rebuild after pushes, run the command from the repository's
`hooks/post-receive` hook. The project includes an example in
`res/hooks/post-receive` that also rebuilds the repository index.

